<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Links of Interest</h2>



<ul class="wp-block-list">

<li>Anne-Laure Le Cunff <a href="https://nesslabs.com/newsletter/difficult-decisions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">looks at what makes a decision difficult</a>, including the difference between needing more information and fearing regret. Her example of accepting a smaller speaking commitment is a useful way to think about protecting writing time.</li>


<li>Cal Newport <a href="https://calnewport.com/in-search-of-the-deep-life/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">introduces the ideas behind The Deep Life</a>. His starting point is that productivity systems need a meaningful life underneath them.</li>


<li>Kourosh Dini <a href="https://www.kouroshdini.com/the-dini-group-ltd-blog/why-tomorrow-is-too-far-away" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">explains why tomorrow can be too far away</a> when you&#8217;re trying to build trust in reminders. He suggests making the first return small and close enough that you&#8217;re likely to meet it.</li>


<li>Federico Viticci <a href="https://www.macstories.net/notes/macos-27-3s-full-disk-access-changes-no-biggie/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">considers the Mac&#8217;s new Full Disk Access controls</a>, including the option to limit access to particular folders. He also raises the question of whether Apple&#8217;s own assistant should face the same permission process.</li>


<li>JazzFuel <a href="https://jazzfuel.com/louis-armstrong-one-night-in-highland-park/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">tells the story behind the newly released Louis Armstrong concert</a>. A student recorded the 1957 performance and kept the tape for almost 70 years. It&#8217;s the recording featured in this week&#8217;s Lab Report.</li>

</ul>



